WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:00.290
<b>The Empty Throne</b>

3
00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.830
Uh, Kaido, sir?

4
00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:15.750
I'm drinking.

5
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.840
You know I don't like to be
interrupted when I'm drinking.

6
00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.090
[BEAST PIRATE A]
Yes, of course, sir!

7
00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:21.800
We all know! But, uh...

8
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:27.010
[Big Mom cackles]

9
00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:31.950
<b>Whole Cake Island</b>

10
00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:36.110
[KAIDO]
What do you want?

11
00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.930
I wanted to give you a warning.

12
00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:42.930
Straw Hat is on his way
to you right now.

13
00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:44.930
[KAIDO]
Is that supposed to scare me?

14
00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:47.940
It shouldn't, if you
keep your hands off him.

15
00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.410
[KAIDO]
Huh?

16
00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:54.260
Just sit tight. I'll head to the Land
of Wano and take care of that brat, myself.

17
00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.140
You gotta be screwing with me! Hell no!

18
00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:00.180
[BIG MOM]
Don't be so sensitive,
it's not about you.

19
00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.270
I have a personal matter
to settle with him,

20
00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:06.330
and if I don't take his head
myself, then I'll lose face.

21
00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:10.390
Beyond that, his crew took something
of mine and I want it back.

22
00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:12.270
[KAIDO]
I don't care!

23
00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:16.010
[BIG MOM]
If I recall,
you owe me a bit of a favor.

24
00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.470
Do I, now?

25
00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.600
[BIG MOM]
Goodness,
don't tell me you've forgotten.

26
00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.600
[KAIDO]
That was a long time ago.

27
00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.930
Maybe so, but it's a lifelong debt.

28
00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.440
[Beast Pirates gasp]

29
00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:37.140
[KAIDO]
Whatever grudge you have against this Straw
Hat kid, I promise you, mine is greater!

30
00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:40.190
[KAIDO]
I'll be the one who kills that punk.

31
00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:43.560
If you test me, Linlin,
I'll kill you, too.

32
00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.260
[BIG MOM]
Try it, then.

33
00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.770
This is a warning.

34
00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:50.810
I didn't call to ask for your opinion.

35
00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:51.940
It's fine!

36
00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:54.820
I'll lop his head off and be done!

37
00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.990
We should be friends!

38
00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:59.820
Just like old times, right?

39
00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:07.420
<b>New Marineford</b>

40
00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:04.680
[MARINE A]
Big Mom is on the move!

41
00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.390
[MARINE B]
Seems like she's
going to meet up with Kaido!

42
00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:09.770
I can't believe they're
using an unsecured channel.

43
00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:12.000
Surely, they knew we'd wiretap them.

44
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.210
What's they're angle?

45
00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.000
Are they trying to provoke us?

46
00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.080
[BIG MOM]
We should be friends,
just like old times, right?

47
00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:22.080
One Emperor is enough trouble,
but two is just plain unmanageable.

48
00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.580
We would need an Admiral,
or a couple Warlords at least.

49
00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:32.270
[KIZARU]
So you want me to
go check it out, Sakazuki?

50
00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.680
[AKAINU]
I think that would be a mistake.

51
00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.810
This is in Wano.

52
00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:40.280
They've got highly-skilled
warriors there.

53
00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:42.660
The samurai, huh?

54
00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.210
<b>The Red Port</b>

55
00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:46.950
[MOMOUSAGI]
Garpie, are you listening?

56
00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:51.430
Kaido and Big Mom are meeting up
and they're going after Straw Hat!

57
00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:54.380
In other words, your grandson.

58
00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.140
That's funny! [laughs]

59
00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.860
I'm afraid I don't see
the humor in this at all!

60
00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.740
Your grandson aside, we can't allow

61
00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:07.140
<b>Vice Admiral Gion (Momousagi)
Marine Headquarters</b>

62
00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.360
two of the Four Emperors to team up!

63
00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:08.940
[GARP]
What do you expect us to do?

64
00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.890
Like it or not, the Reverie's
going on right now.

65
00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:15.400
All our Marines are busy
taking care of royalty.

66
00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.170
[MOMOUSAGI]
So we just sit here?

67
00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.460
[CHATON]
Ain't no coincidence, ma'am!

68
00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.510
We're talking about Big Mom.

69
00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:26.190
She knew dang well we'd be short on soldiers,
otherwise I reckon she wouldn'tve been

70
00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:28.040
<b>Vice Admiral Tokikake (Chaton)
Marine Headquarters</b>

71
00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.050
so bold about this whole business.

72
00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.320
Yes, I'm sure you're right, but still.

73
00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.450
Well, what did the
boss man have to say?

74
00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.490
He said that the Land of Wano
is a non-affiliated country,

75
00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:37.400
so it's outside our jurisdiction.

76
00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.470
I thought so! [laughs]

77
00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:43.020
Better to mind our own business, then!

78
00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.510
I don't know, Garp.

79
00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.300
If Big Mom and Kaido team up,

80
00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:53.400
<b>Rear Admiral Hina
Marine Headquarters</b>

81
00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.640
the Navy will have some major
consequences to deal with.

82
00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.270
And you should know.

83
00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:57.310
They're the reason you were
considered a Navy hero.

84
00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.010
You mean the "Rocks," huh?

85
00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:02.950
Huh?

86
00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:06.870
Funny. I figured you'd be too
young to know about them, Hina.

87
00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:12.760
Before Roger showed up,
it was their era for sure.

88
00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.760
But that was 40 years ago.

89
00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.800
The past is the past.

90
00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.930
They may have lost their captain,
but they're not any weaker for it.

91
00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.670
It worries me a bit.

92
00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:25.000
Eh, it's fine.

93
00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.670
Maybe they'll come back,

94
00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:30.130
but the world's full of "maybes"
and that's what makes it so fun.

95
00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:33.880
Grinning again, are you?
I don't get it.

96
00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:37.940
<b>Pangaea Castle</b>

97
00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:37.940
[SERVANT A]
Enter King Sterry of Goa Kingdom.

98
00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:43.880
[gasps]

99
00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:06.260
[STERRY]
This is it! The center of the world!

100
00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:13.070
[gasps]

101
00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:22.420
Now, make your pledge.

102
00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:25.250
[STERRY]
Huh? Can I sit on the throne first?

103
00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.670
I don't think it's appropriate
to joke about such a thing.

104
00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.660
No man, king or otherwise,
may rest upon that seat.

105
00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:32.360
[STERRY]
Huh?

106
00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:34.150
[SERVANT A]
It's called the Empty Throne.

107
00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:39.490
For all nations of the world are on equal
standing and all rulers must pledge to

108
00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:41.280
respect each other's sovereignty.

109
00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:46.960
The weapons that you see here laid before
the throne were placed there 800 years ago

110
00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.290
to represent an oath made
by the "First Twenty,"

111
00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:51.290
who formed the modern world.

112
00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:55.520
This spot lies at the
very center of the world,

113
00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:59.210
and the fact that none sit upon
the throne is a symbol of peace.

114
00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:03.300
The greatest authority in the government
is held by the Five Elders who are

115
00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:05.640
the highest ranking among
the Celestial Dragons.

116
00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.010
However, even amongst them,
that power is divided.

117
00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:11.980
There is none who would be
called "King of the World."

118
00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:20.230
[SERVANT A]
Now, King Sterry,
it's time to make your pledge.

119
00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:25.110
[STERRY]
If I sit on that chair,
I'll be the boss of everyone!

120
00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.080
Are you feeling ill?

121
00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:31.720
[STERRY]
Let me sit there!

122
00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:33.130
[crowd gasps]

123
00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:34.230
<b>Unity Courtyard
Pangaea Castle</b>

124
00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:34.930
[Shirahoshi screams]

125
00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.930
[SLAVE 3]
C'mon, let's go!

126
00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.670
Get away! Stop!

127
00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:46.260
[Charloss laughs]
I got one! I got one!

128
00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:49.240
<b>Saint Charlos
World Noble (Celestial Dragon)</b>

129
00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:49.100
A big, big mermaid
and she's all mine now!

130
00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:50.350
Shirahoshi! [gasps]

131
00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:52.580
Huh?

132
00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:56.750
We're not stopping him?

133
00:07:56.750 --> 00:08:00.000
I cannot abide by this,
no matter the circumstances!

134
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.130
We must save her!

135
00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:06.260
[SLAVE 3]
That's enough wiggling, Miss fishy!

136
00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.010
Please, stop it!

137
00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.720
[CHARLOSS]
Get those chains on! Hurry it up!

138
00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:14.100
[crowd gasps]

139
00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:15.440
Let her go!

140
00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:17.440
Careful! Stay back, Princess!

141
00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:18.650
You'll get yourself killed that way!

142
00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:20.070
Shirahoshi!

143
00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.360
No, he's a Celestial Dragon. You can't!

144
00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:25.700
Why should I care
about that? Let me go!

145
00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.340
Common sense doesn't apply to them.

146
00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:30.800
They'll burn down every last inch
of Dressrosa if you make them mad!

147
00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:31.850
[gasps]

148
00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.140
That big jerk!

149
00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:41.630
Don't do it, Leo!

150
00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.590
Shirahoshi!

151
00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:53.260
[Shirahoshi crying]

152
00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.980
[WAPOL]
Play it cool, everybody!

153
00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:01.100
[SLAVE 3]
Have it your way!

154
00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.810
[Shirahoshi screams]

155
00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:11.770
[CHARLOSS]
Nice work, Slave 3!

156
00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:15.310
Everyone will be so jealous
when they see my cute new pet!

157
00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:17.780
[crying]

158
00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.110
I can't stand by and watch this!

159
00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:22.740
How dare you do this
to Luffyland's friend!

160
00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:26.000
Leo, no!

161
00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:29.920
Damn it! I guess this is it!

162
00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:32.500
Hold on, I'm coming for you,
Mermaid Princess!

163
00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.710
[ROYAL B]
Someone stop that guy from Kano!

164
00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.130
[ROYAL C]
It's not worth it!

165
00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:37.380
[yells]

166
00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.020
Lemme go!

167
00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:43.270
[screams]

168
00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:46.320
Leo!

169
00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:48.330
Who the hell are you creeps?

170
00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:53.700
<b>Rob Lucci
Cipher Pol 0</b>

171
00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:52.540
I think some gratitude
is in order first.

172
00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:53.580
[Hattori caws]

173
00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:56.030
Cipher Pol 0?

174
00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:59.000
[KAKU]
If we hadn't stopped
your little outburst,

175
00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:01.300
several countries
might have met their end.

176
00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:03.620
<b>Kaku</b>

177
00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.840
Don't stand against
the Celestial Dragons.

178
00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:05.430
Even a kid knows that much.

179
00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.960
<b>Stussy</b>

180
00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:14.230
[NARRATOR]
Cipher Pol is a secretive organization
under the World Government specializing in

181
00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:16.560
intelligence and assassination.

182
00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:20.730
"Aigis" 0 is its most powerful unit,
under the Celestial Dragons.

183
00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:33.910
The Celestial Dragons descended from
the gods who created this world.

184
00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:37.200
Royalty or not, you exist
in a realm beneath them.

185
00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:41.000
If a god desires something of yours,
it must be granted to them.

186
00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:43.710
Finally, one of you morons gets it!

187
00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:46.460
You call this justice?
It doesn't make any sense!

188
00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:48.920
A god is not required to make sense.

189
00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.410
[crowd murmuring]

190
00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:59.980
[NEPTUNE]
Otohime, this can't be
the world you dreamed of

191
00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:02.940
where we would live under
the same sun as humans.

192
00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:06.820
You know this isn't right!
Make him stop it!

193
00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:16.570
[NEPTUNE]
Wait, Princess of Alabasta!

194
00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.200
[ROYAL D]
King Neptune!

195
00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:19.830
[NEPTUNE]
Thank you!

196
00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:22.460
I won't forget your kindness,
brief as our friendship was,

197
00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:26.380
and I'm sorry that
you have to witness this.

198
00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:27.510
[gasps]

199
00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:29.090
[crowd gasps]

200
00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:36.170
[NEPTUNE]
I'll split their skulls and return
to the bottom of the sea for good!

201
00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:38.670
[gasps]

202
00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:39.680
Stop it!

203
00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:41.180
I know how you feel, but you can't!

204
00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:45.380
[NEPTUNE]
If this is what life is like on the surface,
the dream was dead from the start!

205
00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:47.760
[REBECCA]
No, King Neptune! You can't give up!

206
00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:51.130
Don't let the worst examples
of mankind speak for all of us!

207
00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:57.890
[NEPTUNE]
Forgive me, my love.

208
00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:01.040
No! We'll face the humans together!

209
00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:03.440
And maybe then.

210
00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:06.100
We can finally make
a difference for the future,

211
00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:09.600
for our children, for this island...

212
00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:13.560
Even if it's just a small one!

213
00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:19.430
[NEPTUNE]
Even if we bare our hearts
to them, humans won't change!

214
00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:21.770
I must save Shirahoshi!

215
00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:23.110
This is the only way!

216
00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.550
You defy me?

217
00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.600
Cipher Pol, kill him now! Go!

218
00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:28.560
Yes, sir.

219
00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:29.720
[NEPTUNE]
Step aside!

220
00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.890
[ROYAL E]
Please, King Neptune! Listen to reason!

221
00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:34.520
[Neptune yells]

222
00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:36.900
No, Father, please, don't do it!

223
00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:38.270
Please don't give in to hatred!

224
00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:41.400
[Neptune yells]

225
00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:49.510
[NEPTUNE]
Huh?

226
00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:53.840
[crowd gasps]

227
00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:55.420
[ROYAL F]
Someone hit a Celestial Dragon!

228
00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.810
Who was that?

229
00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:58.230
I have nothing to do with this!

230
00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:00.600
Nobody look at me! None of you!

231
00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:01.680
[CROWD]
– Huh?
– Huh?

232
00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:06.860
[Myosgard panting]
As a fellow Celestial Dragon,

233
00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:09.240
I'm ashamed to see such behavior.

234
00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:09.920
[NEPTUNE]
Hm?

235
00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:12.310
[MYOSGARD]
Please forgive us!

236
00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:13.800
[crowd gasps]

237
00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.680
He's a World Noble, too?

238
00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:18.180
[MYOSGARD]
Let go of the princess, you idiot!

239
00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:19.260
[slave 3 gasps]

240
00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:23.540
[MYOSGARD]
My apologies to everyone!

241
00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:26.300
This fool brought savagery
to your peaceful event!

242
00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:32.210
[MYOSGARD]
Since you look surprised, I assume
you don't remember me, Neptune.

243
00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:35.800
But I owe the Ryugu Kingdom
a great debt,

244
00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:38.970
and I have been awaiting
this day for many years.

245
00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:41.930
The day that you would come here.

246
00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:44.600
[Neptune gasps]
No, it can't be.

247
00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:45.680
[gasps]

248
00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:52.610
[MYOSGARD]
I'm a foolish Celestial Dragon, who drifted
down to the Ryugu Kingdom a decade ago,

249
00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:54.110
lost and injured.

250
00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:57.360
I need you to save my life!

251
00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:58.610
Filthy fools!

252
00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:07.280
<b>Saint Donquixote Mjosgard
World Noble (Celestial Dragon)</b>

253
00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:04.450
It was the eloquent words of the late
queen that gave me my humanity.

254
00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:07.320
So now, I will do anything
in my power to aid you!

255
00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:12.910
King Neptune, it is my honor
to welcome you to Mary Geoise!

256
00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:14.290
Go, Cipher Pol!

257
00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:15.620
Retreat from here!

258
00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:28.680
<b>The Holy Land
Mary Geoise</b>

259
00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:32.230
<b>Pangaea Castle</b>

260
00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:40.230
<b>The Room of Authority</b>

261
00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:47.070
<b>The Five Elders
Supreme Council of the World Government</b>

262
00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:50.820
You've traveled quite a long way.

263
00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:52.990
This must be important.

264
00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.780
It's the Reverie now.

265
00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:56.580
Considering your status, I should think

266
00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:59.580
you'd have the sense
to stay out of politics.

267
00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:02.380
But we're willing to honor
your request this time.

268
00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:05.380
[MAN]
Thank you. That's very kind.

269
00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:09.130
Now, then, would you
excuse us for a moment?

270
00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:10.670
[ROYAL GUARDS]
Yes, sir!

271
00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:31.620
I need to speak to you
about a certain pirate.

272
00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:39.330
<b>Unity Courtyard, Pangaea Castle</b>

273
00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:42.480
I'm surprised at
how few people are left.

274
00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:45.190
It's hardly a surprise
after something like that.

275
00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:49.530
I doubt anyone wants to get tangled
up in unwanted trouble, you know?

276
00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:56.160
Wow.

277
00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:57.910
There! All better!

278
00:15:57.910 --> 00:15:59.410
How do you feel?

279
00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:03.120
All of the bruises have
completely disappeared!

280
00:16:03.550 --> 00:16:05.430
Thanks a lot, Mansherry.

281
00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:07.810
That was just like magic!

282
00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:09.600
What a wonderful power!

283
00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:11.570
[giggles]

284
00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:14.440
[Rebecca laughs]
How cute!

285
00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:16.730
The biggest and
the smallest princesses!

286
00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:19.800
It's quite the spectacle
to see you two together!

287
00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:21.840
I'm sorry I was afraid of you.

288
00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:23.680
That was awfully rude of me.

289
00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:25.680
Aww, it's all right, Mansherry.

290
00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:27.680
There's no need to beat yourself up!

291
00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:33.470
[NEPTUNE]
Realistically speaking, all countries
have both good and bad people.

292
00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:37.180
We Fishmen are no exception
to that rule, either!

293
00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:39.420
You have my gratitude, Myosgard.

294
00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:42.240
Thanks to you, I could
keep my promise to Otohime.

295
00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:43.990
There's no need to thank me.

296
00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:48.700
In fact, Neptune, consider this
payment for saving me long ago.

297
00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:53.650
During the seven-day conference,
I promise to look after Princess Shirahoshi.

298
00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:57.870
Honestly, I'm thankful my status is
finally helping someone for once.

299
00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:01.620
So, then I can kick the Celestial Dragons
butts and say that it was an order?

300
00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:04.020
I was told I was supposed to
keep my hands off of them,

301
00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:06.120
but if you give me permission...

302
00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.880
Oh. Sure!

303
00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:10.400
I will gladly take
responsibility for that!

304
00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:13.320
Please, do what you must
to protect the princess!

305
00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:17.300
Now, ain't that something.

306
00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:20.420
It's hard to believe
one of 'em's got a heart.

307
00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:22.630
Princess Vivi!

308
00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:26.050
My most sincere apologies.

309
00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:27.260
Are you all right?

310
00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:28.810
I heard that there was some trouble.

311
00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.980
Sorry, I should have
never left your side.

312
00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:34.290
Don't worry, Pell. I'm doing fine.

313
00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:36.320
Anyway, how's my father?

314
00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.570
[PELL]
King Cobra's occupied at the moment.

315
00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:39.860
He's with Fujitora.

316
00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:42.070
That one Admiral who sent the letter.

317
00:17:42.070 --> 00:17:43.950
He wants to speak to King Riku.

318
00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:44.970
Let's give them time.

319
00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:51.970
<b>Pangaea Castle</b>

320
00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:51.730
[NARRATOR]
Pangaea Castle.

321
00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:54.690
It has three entryways
outside of its main gate,

322
00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:57.400
all of which are heavily guarded.

323
00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:02.520
[NARRATOR]
One of those gates belongs
to the Celestial Dragons.

324
00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:06.060
It leads to the Land of the Gods
where these nobles reside.

325
00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:17.420
[ROYAL GUARD G]
Stop! State your name!

326
00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:21.170
[chuckling]

327
00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:21.710
<b>Queen Dowager Conney
Kingdom of Sorbet</b>

328
00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:25.300
[ROYAL GUARD H]
Why, it's Queen Dowager
Conney of the Sorbet Kingdom!

329
00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:27.130
Hello, ma'am.

330
00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:30.930
[chuckles]

331
00:18:30.930 --> 00:18:33.420
[ROYAL GUARD H]
The Land of
the Gods lies beyond this point.

332
00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:36.210
I'm afraid that it's far too
dangerous for you to proceed.

333
00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:38.010
Please return to the castle.

334
00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:42.520
[CHARLOSS]
The pain! This is unforgivable!

335
00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:44.100
Damn that Myosgard!

336
00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:46.860
[ROYAL BODYGUARD A]
Saint Charloss! Please calm down!

337
00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:48.820
You'll open your wounds!

338
00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:52.860
That man will pay. Mark my words!

339
00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:54.060
Hey, open the gate!

340
00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:57.740
[ROYAL GUARD H]
Huh? What's going on here?

341
00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:00.120
[ROYAL BODYGUARD A]
Saint Charloss is injured!

342
00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:02.990
He needs medical
assistance immediately!

343
00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:04.450
[ROYAL GUARD G]
Right away!

344
00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:15.860
[ROYAL GUARD C]
Move it! To the doctor!

345
00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:23.030
My goodness, Charloss!

346
00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:25.390
<b>Saint Rosward
World Noble (Celestial Dragon)</b>

347
00:19:23.030 --> 00:19:25.660
How are you fairing
after your recent incident?

348
00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:27.330
Oh, my poor boy.

349
00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:30.290
After I heard the news,
I rushed over to get you!

350
00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:32.170
Saint Roswald! Sir!

351
00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:35.170
Huh? Father, is that you?

352
00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:39.800
[ROSWALD]
Tell me, how did this happen?

353
00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:43.220
Oh, my beloved son!

354
00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:50.960
[ROYAL GUARD H]
Huh? Where's the Queen Dowager?

355
00:19:51.990 --> 00:19:56.160
That blasted Don Quixote
Myosgard must pay!

356
00:19:58.010 --> 00:20:01.180
[ROSWALD]
Unreal! What kind of Celestial Dragon
refuses to keep even a single slave?

357
00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:05.480
He's just like that kook Homing who
descended to the lower world 30 years ago.

358
00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:08.460
The Don Quixote Family has some nerve.

359
00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:10.510
That big bunch of lunatics!

360
00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:13.220
[gasps]
I didn't realize, Father!

361
00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:15.010
You brought him?

362
00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:20.530
<b>Warlord Bartholomew Kuma
(Former Revolutionary Officer)
(Former King of Sorbet)</b>

363
00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:20.530
[CHARLOSS]
The invincible slave, Kuma!

364
00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:22.350
Well, of course I did!

365
00:20:22.350 --> 00:20:27.310
It was finally my long-awaited turn
to take him for a spin on the rental list.

366
00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:30.270
Wow, that's great!

367
00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:32.980
The invincible slave
makes a fine steed, Father.

368
00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:34.810
The wait was surely worth it!

369
00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:38.440
Who knew a Warlord would make such
a fine mode of transportation!

370
00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:40.760
And it's so much fun to hit him!

371
00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:43.010
[ROSWALD]
You can stab him, too!

372
00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.390
He doesn't scream either.

373
00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:50.520
He's truly the finest
slave of them all!

374
00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:52.640
[CHARLOSS]
He's glorious, Father!

375
00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:55.400
I want one, too!

376
00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:56.990
Ow, ow, ow.

377
00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.320
If I don't die first!

378
00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:02.320
Are you okay, sir? Let's keep it down.

379
00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:06.740
I've really had a rotten time
since everyone got here.

380
00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:09.120
[ROSWALD]
Oh, my poor Charloss!

381
00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:14.130
Let's summon the world's greatest
physician to fix you up, shall we?

382
00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:21.510
[BONNEY]
I didn't expect to run into
him out in the open like that!

383
00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:32.060
<b>Captain Jewelry Bonney
Bonney Pirates
A Pirate of the Worst Generation</b>

384
00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:32.180
[BONNEY]
At least I made it inside.

385
00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:39.910
[BONNEY]
I'll make sure they all pay.

386
00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:45.170
[BONNEY]
I swear it!

387
00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:51.330
[SABO]
Dammit!

388
00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:58.300
<b>Beneath the Land of the Gods, Home of the Celestial Dragons</b>

389
00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:55.050
[MORLEY]
Cool your jets, Sabo.

390
00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:58.870
Golly, you boys can be so scary!

391
00:21:58.870 --> 00:22:01.110
[SABO]
You're telling me you're not angy?

392
00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:04.030
You saw what those monsters
are doing to our comrade!

393
00:22:04.030 --> 00:22:06.950
They're torturing that
poor, kindhearted man!

394
00:22:07.950 --> 00:22:11.670
[SABO]
They'll pay for this.

395
00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:15.160
[KARASU]
Calm down.

396
00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:18.670
We feel you. It really is terrible.

397
00:22:18.670 --> 00:22:21.420
I promise that we won't
leave Kuma in that state!

398
00:22:21.420 --> 00:22:24.700
[KARASU]
After all,
that's the reason we're here.

399
00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:27.410
[KARASU]
The problem is, even if we free him,

400
00:22:27.750 --> 00:22:32.130
I'm afraid he won't
return to his former self.

401
00:22:33.890 --> 00:22:37.650
All his life, Kuma was a victim
of the World Government's oppression

402
00:22:37.650 --> 00:22:39.820
in one way or another.

403
00:22:39.820 --> 00:22:41.570
They made an example out of him.

404
00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:43.370
It was a warning, right?

405
00:22:43.370 --> 00:22:47.220
"No one's safe from us.
Even kings of allied nations."

406
00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:52.430
Those who defy the gods will all be
brought to their knees, without question.

407
00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:55.770
They have the whole Navy
and CP-0 on their side.

408
00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:57.560
More than anyone can handle.

409
00:22:57.560 --> 00:22:59.730
We can't screw up and get caught.

410
00:22:59.730 --> 00:23:02.480
I know. We won't.

411
00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:04.530
Either we succeed or die.

412
00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:15.210
[NARRATOR]
And so, the much-anticipated event,

413
00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:17.290
<b>The Holy Land, Mary Geoise</b>

414
00:23:15.210 --> 00:23:18.800
the Reverie, commences!

415
00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:20.710
<b>Pangaea Castle</b>

416
00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:20.260
[NARRATOR]
The seas of the world are divided

417
00:23:20.260 --> 00:23:21.420
into four bodies of water.

418
00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:33.680
<b>East Blue North Blue</b>
<b>New World</b>
<b>Mary
Geoise</b>
<b>South Blue West Blue</b>

419
00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:25.050
They are split one way by a massive
continental wall known as the Red Line,

420
00:23:25.640 --> 00:23:29.640
and split the other way by a dangerous
stretch of sea known as the Grand Line.

421
00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:34.150
Within these waters lies the New
World, where Luffy is traveling.

422
00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:37.070
[NARRATOR]
The World Government
is a massive organization,

423
00:23:37.070 --> 00:23:42.650
encompassing most of the world's
nations, 170 in total.

424
00:23:43.160 --> 00:23:46.620
[NARRATOR]
Every four years, 50 chosen
rulers are sent to this Holy Land

425
00:23:46.620 --> 00:23:50.750
to represent their nations
in important negotiations.

426
00:23:57.670 --> 00:23:59.580
Which one is my seat?

427
00:24:01.750 --> 00:24:02.880
[Sterry gasps]

428
00:24:07.480 --> 00:24:09.020
At long last.

429
00:24:09.020 --> 00:24:10.770
[LEMONCHEESE]
Indeed. Tell me.

430
00:24:10.770 --> 00:24:12.270
How's your country been?

431
00:24:12.270 --> 00:24:15.610
You said pirates left it
in ruin four years ago.

432
00:24:15.610 --> 00:24:17.400
They're locked up in Impel Down.

433
00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:19.740
Courtesy of Fleet Admiral Sakazuki.

434
00:24:19.740 --> 00:24:25.400
Which reminds me, who is this boy I keep
hearing about in the news? You know.

435
00:24:25.400 --> 00:24:27.640
You mean Straw Hat Luffy?

436
00:24:27.640 --> 00:24:29.760
He made an attempt on Big Mom's life,

437
00:24:30.990 --> 00:24:34.160
and it's rumored that he has
his sights set on Kaido next.

438
00:24:34.160 --> 00:24:35.460
Fancy that!

439
00:24:35.460 --> 00:24:37.000
The Emperor?

440
00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:39.940
Then I wonder what's going to
happen in the Land of Wano.

441
00:24:39.940 --> 00:24:41.940
They don't participate
in the World Government,

442
00:24:41.940 --> 00:24:45.760
so needless to say,
it's practically a lawless land.

443
00:24:45.760 --> 00:24:48.390
If that's the case,
I must raise the question.

444
00:24:48.390 --> 00:24:50.720
Can we even consider them a nation?

445
00:24:50.720 --> 00:24:53.680
Perhaps we should make
that our business then?

446
00:24:54.230 --> 00:24:56.370
It's hardly that simple.

447
00:24:56.370 --> 00:24:58.250
The Navy costs money.

448
00:25:02.490 --> 00:25:06.760
Trouble seems to follow that Straw Hat
Luffy wherever he goes, doesn't it?

449
00:25:06.760 --> 00:25:08.710
He sounds like a pain.

450
00:25:08.710 --> 00:25:11.510
Tell me about it! [laughs]

451
00:25:11.510 --> 00:25:13.800
[COBRA]
What's so funny, Prodence?

452
00:25:14.200 --> 00:25:16.240
[COBRA]
Luffy.

453
00:25:17.130 --> 00:25:19.420
As always, we have a new chairman.

454
00:25:19.420 --> 00:25:21.950
Who's up now?

455
00:25:21.950 --> 00:25:23.580
It's me!

456
00:25:23.580 --> 00:25:25.870
Hello there, everyone.

457
00:25:25.870 --> 00:25:27.600
It's Ballywood, huh?

458
00:25:27.600 --> 00:25:29.100
Greetings.

459
00:25:29.100 --> 00:25:32.640
Excellent. He'll run this efficiently.

460
00:25:32.640 --> 00:25:33.890
Let's get started.

461
00:25:33.890 --> 00:25:36.530
We have quite a lot to address.

462
00:25:36.530 --> 00:25:40.580
[NARRATOR]
The most influential rulers in all
four seas begin their discussions.

463
00:25:40.580 --> 00:25:43.830
Together, they will reshape the world.

464
00:25:44.870 --> 00:25:48.750
Now! Without further ado,
let's commence the debate.

465
00:25:49.610 --> 00:25:54.520
For seven days, my fellow noblemen,
we shall speak of this beautiful world of ours!

466
00:26:01.080 --> 00:26:02.500
[NARRATOR]
This is the Reverie!

467
00:26:03.790 --> 00:26:06.880
[ELDER STAR D]
It seems like the conference has begun.

468
00:26:07.130 --> 00:26:08.590
While on that subject.

469
00:26:08.590 --> 00:26:14.010
Cobra, the king of Alabasta,
is requesting a special meeting with us.

470
00:26:14.010 --> 00:26:15.930
The Nefertari Family, huh?

471
00:26:15.930 --> 00:26:17.260
How interesting.

472
00:26:17.260 --> 00:26:19.220
They were the only family
of the First Twenty

473
00:26:19.720 --> 00:26:22.690
who stayed in the lower world
800 years ago.

474
00:26:22.690 --> 00:26:25.190
So then in a sense, they're traitors.

475
00:26:25.190 --> 00:26:27.520
Has he noticed something out of sorts?

476
00:26:27.520 --> 00:26:30.570
Let's hope he doesn't
overcomplicate things for us.

477
00:26:31.090 --> 00:26:32.470
Worrisome times.

478
00:26:32.470 --> 00:26:34.720
Big Mom and Kaido are trouble.

479
00:26:34.720 --> 00:26:40.770
This started with the War of the Best,
and now, I fear it can't be stopped.

480
00:26:40.770 --> 00:26:44.890
[ELDER STAR D]
The balance of the world
can't be maintained forever.

481
